cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VSArena"
message: "If you use VSArena in research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "NovaCoding-G"
    email: "novacodingg@gmail.com"
    website: "https://github.com/NovaCoding-G"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NovaCoding-G/VSArena"
url: "https://github.com/NovaCoding-G/VSArena"
abstract: >-
  VSArena is an open, browser-based stacking work-cell and evaluation harness
  for Vision-Language-Action (VLA) and embodied agents. Policies receive RGB
  and a language instruction; scoring and public ELO are written by a trusted
  harness, not the browser.
keywords:
  - embodied AI
  - VLA
  - robotics
  - benchmark
  - simulation
  - leaderboard
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-21"
